---
import StaticSubmissionForm from "../components/StaticSubmissionForm.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Supplier listing update"
  description="Supply current first-party information for an existing Church Software UK listing without influencing its independent assessment."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Supplier listing update" }]}
>
  <section class="section submission-page">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="submission-lead">
        <p class="eyebrow">Supplier information</p>
        <h1>Supplier listing update</h1>
        <p>
          Suppliers can point us to current first-party information. Evidence may
          lead to an update, clarification or no change; it does not buy inclusion,
          ranking or favourable editorial coverage.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="prose measure">
        <h2>Useful supplier evidence</h2>
        <p>Link to public, current first-party pages and identify the exact field affected. The most useful evidence concerns UK purchasing, pricing and VAT, Gift Aid or payment workflow, data-processing information, exports, migration, permissions, support and cancellation terms.</p>
        <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
        <p>We welcome corrections and clarifications, but product inclusion and assessment remain independent. We may update a published fact, qualify it more clearly, retain an open question or decide that the evidence does not support a change. Do not include customer, church-member, pastoral, safeguarding or financial data.</p>
        <p>If the information is time-sensitive, include the published date or a clear statement that the linked page is current. A public source makes it possible for churches to check the same detail later and keeps the correction process transparent.</p>
      </div>
      <StaticSubmissionForm kind="supplier" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
